In article <90040213364957@masnet.uucp> ted.ho@canremote.uucp (TED HO) writes:
>I have an Amiga 500 with 1Meg on board and two floppy drives.  I was 
>ecstatic to see NetHack 3.0.  However, happiness turned to 
>dissappointment when I discovered I could not proceed beyond level one 
>of the dungeon due to lack of disk space.  Does anyone with a similar 
>setup have a solution?
>
>Thanks
>---
> * Via ProDoor 3.1R 


I have a third disk set up with my character and the levels stored to
it.  I named the disk "HackDisk:".  I made a bones and a save directory
and I set up the following options in NetHack.cnf -

HACKDIR=NetHack:
LEVELS=HackDisk:bones
SAVE=HackDisk:save
RAMDISK=HackDisk: 

Probably that last entry could be done differently, but it accomplished
my purpose, which was to have the intermediate levels during the game to
be stored on my HackDisk:.

After the game loads remove the HackExe: disk from df1: and replace
it with HackDisk:.


Good luck!
